### V-003: Missing Authorization

**Vulnerability ID:** V-003  
**Title:** No Role-Based Access Control  
**Severity:** 🔴 HIGH  
**CVSS v3.1 Score:** 8.6  
**CWE:** CWE-639: Authorization Bypass Through User-Controlled Key  
**OWASP:** A01:2021 – Broken Access Control

#### Description
Even with authentication, there's no authorization check to ensure users can only access data they're permitted to see.

#### Vulnerable Code
```javascript
// VULNERABLE - assumes all authenticated users can access /users
app.get('/users', authenticateToken, (req, res) => {
  res.json([...allUsers]); // No role check
});
```

#### Attack Scenario
```
1. Regular user logs in
2. Obtains JWT token
3. Accesses /users endpoint
4. Receives all user data (should only see own profile)
```

#### Remediation

**Solution: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)**
```javascript
const requireAdmin = (req, res, next) => {
  if (!req.user || req.user.role !== 'admin') {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Admin required' });
  }
  next();
};

const allowOwnData = (req, res, next) => {
  if (req.user.id !== parseInt(req.params.id) && req.user.role !== 'admin') {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Access denied' });
  }
  next();
};

// Only admins can view all users
app.get('/users', authenticateToken, requireAdmin, (req, res) => {
  res.json([...allUsers]);
});

// Users can only view their own profile
app.get('/users/:id', authenticateToken, allowOwnData, (req, res) => {
  res.json(getUserById(req.params.id));
});
```

#### Implementation Checklist
- [ ] Define roles (user, admin, moderator, etc.)
- [ ] Create authorization middleware
- [ ] Implement permission checks
- [ ] Add role to JWT payload
- [ ] Store roles in database
- [ ] Test authorization logic
- [ ] Document permission matrix

