### V-005: No Input Validation

**Vulnerability ID:** V-005  
**Title:** Missing Input Validation and Sanitization  
**Severity:** 🔴 HIGH  
**CVSS v3.1 Score:** 7.8  
**CWE:** CWE-20: Improper Input Validation  
**OWASP:** A03:2021 – Injection

#### Description
Application does not validate or sanitize user input, vulnerable to:
- SQL/NoSQL injection
- XSS attacks
- Command injection
- Path traversal

#### Vulnerable Code
```javascript
// VULNERABLE - no validation
app.post('/login', (req, res) => {
  const { email, password } = req.body;
  // Use email and password directly without validation
  authenticateUser(email, password);
});
```

#### Attack Examples

**NoSQL Injection:**
```javascript
// Attacker sends:
POST /login
{"email": {"$ne": null}, "password": {"$ne": null}}

// Becomes MongoDB query:
db.users.findOne({
  email: {$ne: null},   // Matches any user!
  password: {$ne: null}
})
```

**XSS Attack:**
```javascript
// Attacker sends:
POST /profile
{"name": "<img src=x onerror='alert(1)'>"}

// Gets stored and rendered in response
```

#### Remediation

**Solution: Input Validation**
```javascript
const { body, validationResult } = require('express-validator');

app.post('/login', [
  body('email')
    .isEmail()
    .normalizeEmail()
    .withMessage('Invalid email'),
  body('password')
    .isLength({ min: 8, max: 128 })
    .matches(/^[a-zA-Z0-9!@#$%^&*]/)
    .withMessage('Invalid password format'),
], (req, res) => {
  const errors = validationResult(req);
  if (!errors.isEmpty()) {
    return res.status(400).json({ errors: errors.array() });
  }

  const { email, password } = req.body;
  authenticateUser(email, password);
});

// Sanitization
const mongoSanitize = require('express-mongo-sanitize');
app.use(mongoSanitize());
```

