### V-007: No Error Handling

**Vulnerability ID:** V-007  
**Title:** Unhandled Errors and Information Disclosure  
**Severity:** 🟡 MEDIUM  
**CVSS v3.1 Score:** 6.2  
**CWE:** CWE-209: Information Exposure Through an Error Message  
**OWASP:** A01:2021 – Broken Access Control

#### Description
Uncaught exceptions expose internal error details, stack traces, and system information to attackers.

#### Vulnerable Code
```javascript
// VULNERABLE - no error handling
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  const users = getUsersFromDB(); // Could throw
  res.json(users);
});
```

#### Information Leakage Example
```
Error: Cannot find module 'postgresql'
at Object.<anonymous> (/app/db.js:5:10)
at Module._load (internal/modules/loaded_as_modules.js:1337:20)
at require (internal/modules/loaded_as_modules.js:1265:5)
at Object.<anonymous> (/app/app.js:3:10)

^ Reveals application structure, node version, file paths
```

#### Remediation

**Solution: Error Handling Middleware**
```javascript
// Route-level error handling
app.get('/users', async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const users = await getUsersFromDB();
    res.json(users);
  } catch (error) {
    logger.error(`Error fetching users: ${error.message}`);
    next(error); // Pass to global handler
  }
});

// Global error handler (must be last)
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  logger.error({
    error: err.message,
    stack: err.stack,
    path: req.path,
    method: req.method
  });

  const isProduction = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production';

  res.status(err.statusCode || 500).json({
    error: isProduction ? 'Internal server error' : err.message,
    ...(isProduction ? {} : { stack: err.stack })
  });
});

// 404 handler
app.use((req, res) => {
  res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' });
});
```

#### Implementation Checklist
