- **Fix:** Add authentication and authorization middleware

### A02: Cryptographic Failures
- **Status:** ❌ Not Implemented
- **Risk:** Unencrypted data in transit and at rest
- **Fix:** Enable HTTPS, encrypt sensitive data

### A03: Injection
- **Status:** ⚠️ Partially Vulnerable
- **Risk:** SQL/NoSQL injection, command injection
- **Fix:** Use parameterized queries, validate input

### A04: Insecure Design
- **Status:** ⚠️ Partially Vulnerable
- **Risk:** Missing security features
- **Fix:** Implement security patterns from design phase

### A05: Security Misconfiguration
- **Status:** ❌ Not Implemented
- **Risk:** Exposed configuration, default settings
- **Fix:** Configure security headers, logging, monitoring

### A06: Vulnerable Components
- **Status:** ⚠️ Depends on Dependencies
- **Risk:** Outdated packages with known vulnerabilities
- **Fix:** Run `npm audit`, keep packages updated

### A07: Authentication Failures
- **Status:** ❌ Not Implemented
- **Risk:** Weak or missing authentication
- **Fix:** Implement JWT with proper validation

### A08: Data Integrity Failures
- **Status:** ⚠️ Partially Vulnerable
- **Risk:** Unverified data updates
- **Fix:** Add data validation and integrity checks

### A09: Logging Failures
- **Status:** ❌ Not Implemented
- **Risk:** Can't detect or investigate attacks
- **Fix:** Add comprehensive logging

### A10: SSRF
- **Status:** ✅ Not Applicable
- **Risk:** Limited scope of current application
- **Fix:** If added in future, validate all URLs

---

## Testing Checklist

Before considering your app secure, test for:

### Functional Tests
- [ ] All endpoints return expected responses
- [ ] Authentication works correctly
- [ ] Authorization blocks unauthorized access
- [ ] Input validation rejects invalid data

### Security Tests
- [ ] No console.log or debug info exposed
- [ ] Stack traces not exposed in errors
- [ ] Security headers present
- [ ] HTTPS enforced
- [ ] Rate limiting working

### Attack Scenario Tests
- [ ] SQL Injection attempts rejected
- [ ] XSS payloads blocked
- [ ] CSRF token validated
- [ ] NoSQL injection attempts rejected
- [ ] Brute force attempts rate limited

### Integration Tests
- [ ] Database queries use parameterized statements
- [ ] Environment variables properly isolated
- [ ] Secrets not in logs
- [ ] Monitoring/alerting working

---

## Deployment Checklist

### Pre-Deployment
- [ ] All security tests pass
- [ ] npm audit shows no critical issues
- [ ] Environment variables configured
- [ ] Secrets in secrets manager, not in code
- [ ] SSL certificate installed
- [ ] Firewall rules updated

### Deployment
- [ ] Deploy to production environment
- [ ] Verify all endpoints accessible
- [ ] Check logs for errors
- [ ] Monitor for unusual activity
- [ ] Test authentication/authorization

### Post-Deployment
- [ ] Monitor error rates
- [ ] Check security logs
- [ ] Verify backups working
- [ ] Test incident response procedures
- [ ] Document any issues found

---

## Common Vulnerabilities to Avoid

### ❌ DON'T

```javascript
// Hardcode secrets
const SECRET = "my-secret-key";

// Trust user input
app.get('/search', (req, res) => {
  const query = req.query.q;
  db.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '${query}'`); // SQL Injection!
});

// Expose stack traces
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  res.json(err); // Exposes everything!
});

// Send sensitive data
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json({
    id: 1,
    name: 'Alice',
    password: 'alice123', // NEVER!
    ssn: '123-45-6789' // NEVER!
  });
});

// Use eval or similar
eval(userInput); // NEVER!

// Trust headers blindly
app.get('/admin', (req, res) => {
  if (req.headers['x-is-admin'] === 'true') { // Client can fake this!
    res.json({ admin: true });
  }
});
```

### ✅ DO

```javascript
// Use environment variables
const SECRET = process.env.JWT_SECRET;

// Validate and parameterize
app.get('/search', (req, res) => {
  const query = req.query.q;
  if (!query || query.length > 100) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid query' });
  }
  db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = ?', [query]); // Safe!
});

// Handle errors securely
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  logger.error(err); // Log securely
  res.json({ error: 'Internal error' }); // Generic message
});

// Filter sensitive data
app.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => {
  const user = getUser(req.params.id);
  res.json({
    id: user.id,
    name: user.name
    // password and ssn omitted
  });
});

// Use safe methods
app.post('/data', (req, res) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(req.body); // Safer than eval
});

// Verify with tokens/sessions
app.get('/admin', authenticate, authorize('admin'), (req, res) => {
  res.json({ admin: true });
});
```

---

## Performance vs Security Trade-offs

| Feature | Performance | Security | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|---|
| JWT Expiration | High (short expires) | High | Set to 24h |
| Rate Limiting | Medium | High | Required |
| Request Size Limits | High | High | 10KB default |
| HTTPS | Low | High | Required |
| Input Validation | Medium | High | Required |
| Encryption | Low | High | For sensitive data |
| Logging | Low | Medium | Async logging |

---

