## Summary

| Vulnerability | Impact | Fix |
|---------------|--------|-----|
| No Authentication | Anyone can access private data | Add JWT middleware |
| Exposed Credentials | Complete system compromise | Use secrets manager |
| No Input Validation | Injection attacks | Use express-validator |
| Missing Security Headers | XSS, Clickjacking, etc. | Use helmet middleware |
| No Rate Limiting | Brute force, DoS | Use express-rate-limit |
| No Error Handling | Information disclosure | Use error middleware |
| Broken CORS | CSRF attacks | Configure CORS whitelist |
| No HTTPS | Man-in-the-middle attacks | Use TLS/SSL |
| SQL Injection | Database compromise | Use parameterized queries |
| XSS | Account hijacking | Escape/sanitize output |
| Data Exposure | Privacy violation | Return only necessary fields |
| Hardcoded Secrets | Credential theft | Use environment variables |

All of these vulnerabilities are addressed in **app.secure.js** and tests are provided in **security.test.js**.

