## A01:2021 - Broken Access Control

### Vulnerabilities Found

1. **No authentication/authorization checks**
   - All endpoints publicly accessible
   - No role-based access control
   - Sensitive data exposed to anyone

2. **Unrestricted user access**
   - `/users` endpoint returns all user data
   - No filtering based on user permissions

### Fixes Applied

```javascript
// ❌ BEFORE - No access control
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ]);
});

// ✅ AFTER - With authentication and authorization
const authMiddleware = (req, res, next) => {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
  if (!token) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Unauthorized' });

  try {
    req.user = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
    next();
  } catch (e) {
    res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
  }
};

const requireRole = (roles) => (req, res, next) => {
  if (!roles.includes(req.user.role)) {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Insufficient permissions' });
  }
  next();
};

app.get('/api/users', authMiddleware, requireRole(['user', 'admin']), (req, res) => {
  const users = [...];
  const sanitized = users.map(u => ({
    id: u.id,
    name: u.name,
    ...(req.user.role === 'admin' && { email: u.email })
  }));
  res.json(sanitized);
});

app.get('/api/admin/users', authMiddleware, requireRole(['admin']), (req, res) => {
  // Only admins can see all data
  res.json([...]);
});
```

### Implementation Checklist

- [ ] Implement JWT authentication
- [ ] Add role-based access control (RBAC)
- [ ] Implement access level checks on all endpoints
- [ ] Filter responses based on user permissions
- [ ] Log all access control violations
- [ ] Implement account separation (users can't access others' data)
- [ ] Use principle of least privilege

