## Vulnerability #8: No HTTPS

### ❌ VULNERABLE (Original app.js)
```javascript
const app = express();

app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});

// Connection is HTTP (not encrypted)! 
// 
// Attack vectors:
// - Man-in-the-middle can read all traffic ✗
// - Authentication tokens can be stolen ✗
// - User passwords visible in plaintext ✗
// - Any sensitive data exposed ✗
// 
// curl http://localhost:3000/users
// All data sent unencrypted over the network! ✗
```

### ✅ SECURE (app-secure.js)
```javascript
const https = require('https');
const fs = require('fs');

const app = express();

if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
  // Load SSL certificates
  const options = {
    key: fs.readFileSync(process.env.SSL_KEY),
    cert: fs.readFileSync(process.env.SSL_CERT)
  };

  // Create HTTPS server
  https.createServer(options, app).listen(3000, () => {
    console.log('Secure server running on port 3000 (HTTPS)');
  });

  // Redirect HTTP to HTTPS
  const http = require('http');
  http.createServer((req, res) => {
    res.writeHead(301, { 
      Location: `https://${req.headers.host}${req.url}` 
    });
    res.end();
  }).listen(80);
} else {
  app.listen(3000);
}

// Now connection is HTTPS (encrypted)! ✓
// curl https://localhost:3000/users
// All data encrypted in transit ✓
// 
// Security improvements:
// - All traffic encrypted ✓
// - Man-in-the-middle protection ✓
// - Authentication tokens secure ✓
// - Passwords protected ✓
// - Complies with security standards ✓
```

