## Environment-Specific Configuration

### .gitignore (Add These Lines)

```bash
# Environment variables
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Private keys
*.key
*.pem
*.p12

# AWS credentials
.aws/
AWS_*

# Sensitive logs
error.log
combined.log
*.log

# IDE secrets
.idea/workspace.xml
.vscode/settings.json
```

### .env.example (Never commit real secrets)

```bash
# IMPORTANT: This is a TEMPLATE only
# NEVER commit actual secret values
# NEVER copy this to .env in production

# Authentication
JWT_SECRET=your-dev-secret-key-change-in-production-DO-NOT-USE-IN-PROD
ENCRYPTION_KEY=your-dev-encryption-key-32-chars-long-minimum

# For production, use AWS Secrets Manager, Azure Key Vault, or similar
# Set VAULT_ADDR or SECRETS_NAME instead of actual secrets

# Configuration (not secrets)
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
LOG_LEVEL=debug
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# Production Secrets Manager (if using one)
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# SECRETS_NAME=prod/app/secrets
# 
# Or for Vault:
# VAULT_ADDR=https://vault.example.com:8200
# VAULT_TOKEN=<authenticated-token>
```

