### 5. ❌ HIGH: Sensitive Data Exposure (OWASP A01:2021 - Broken Access Control)

**Severity**: HIGH

**Issue**:
- User emails are hardcoded and exposed without authentication
- If expanded, could expose passwords, tokens, or other PII
- No data filtering based on user permissions

**Recommended Fix**:
```javascript
app.get('/users', authenticateToken, (req, res) => {
  // Only return non-sensitive fields for regular users
  if (req.user.role !== 'admin') {
    return res.json([
      { id: 1, name: 'Alice' }, // No email
      { id: 2, name: 'Bob' },
    ]);
  }

  // Admin can see all data
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ]);
});

// Separate endpoint for individual user data (with proper checks)
app.get('/users/:id', authenticateToken, (req, res) => {
  const userId = parseInt(req.params.id, 10);

  // Validate parameter
  if (isNaN(userId) || userId < 1) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid user ID' });
  }

  // Ensure user can only view their own data or admin views all
  if (req.user.id !== userId && req.user.role !== 'admin') {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
  }

  // Return user data
  const user = { id: userId, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' };
  res.json(user);
});
