# Security Review: Before & After Comparison

## Original Code (VULNERABLE)

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();

app.get('/health', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ status: 'ok', timestamp: new Date().toISOString() });
});

app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ]);
});

app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});

module.exports = app;
```

## Issues Found

### ❌ CRITICAL: No Authentication
**Risk**: Anyone can access user data without any authorization

### ❌ CRITICAL: No Input Validation  
**Risk**: SQL injection, XSS, command injection possible

### ❌ CRITICAL: No HTTPS
**Risk**: Data transmitted unencrypted over HTTP

### ❌ HIGH: Sensitive Data Exposed
**Risk**: User emails visible without authentication

### ❌ HIGH: No Security Headers
**Risk**: Vulnerable to clickjacking, XSS, MIME-sniffing

### ❌ HIGH: No Rate Limiting
**Risk**: Vulnerable to brute force and DoS attacks

### ❌ MEDIUM: No CORS Configuration
**Risk**: Unclear which origins are allowed/denied

### ❌ MEDIUM: No Error Handling
**Risk**: Stack traces may expose system information

### ❌ MEDIUM: No Logging
**Risk**: Cannot detect or investigate security incidents

### ❌ MEDIUM: No Environment Validation
**Risk**: Missing configuration could cause failures

